        "original_id": "4941cd0b-0b7a-50d9-9188-2092062c57e0",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: George Armistead\n- Places: Fort McHenry, Baltimore, Maryland, Baltimore Harbor, Chesapeake Bay\n- Roles: American military officer, commander\n- Events: Battle of Baltimore, War of 1812, World War I, World War II\n- Organizations: U.S. armed forces, Coast Guard\n\nFacts:\n- Fort McHenry was first built in 1798.\n- George Armistead was born on April 10, 1780, and died on April 25, 1818.\n- George Armistead was an American military officer who served as the commander of Fort McHenry during the Battle of Baltimore in the War of 1812.\n- On September 13–14, 1814, Fort McHenry successfully defended Baltimore Harbor from an attack by the British navy from the Chesapeake Bay during the War of 1812.\n- Fort McHenry is a historic American coastal pentagonal bastion fort in Baltimore, Maryland.\n- Fort McHenry was used continuously by U.S. armed forces through World War I and by the Coast Guard in World War II.",
